*** This is free software with ABSOLUTELY NO WARRANTY ***

I thought about GPLing this software but to be honest I want a bit more
control over what happens to it. I'll probably agree to most things with
respect to the code but please ask first!

COMPILING:
This software has only been tested on Linux, FreeBSD and Solaris (using gcc).
The odds are it won't compile or run properly on other versions of Unix though
other versions of *BSD should be ok.

Cd to "src" and then:

Linux/BSD: Just type "make"
Solaris  : Uncomment DEFS in the makefile then type "make"

Once compiled just type "./basic" to run the interpreter.

Documentation is in DOCS/ and examples BASIC programs are in progs/

To load an example program (eg bounce.bas) either type 
-run "../progs/bounce.bas" on the command line or enter 
load "../progs/bounce.bas" then "run" inside the interpreter.

NOTES:
The cursor on/off function doesn't work properly on BSD console
screens. You make see part of the ANSI command code printed out as
plain text.

The scroll command doesn't work on Linux consoles.


